ðŸ“¦ Patch Notes â€” Release 2026-01-21
ðŸ›¡ï¸ Critical Bug Fixes & Stability Hardening
- **Dead Player Ultimate Exploit**: Fixed critical exploit where dead players could activate ultimate abilities while spectating.
- **Mage Crash Fix**: Fixed NullReferenceException in ManaShieldEffect.OnStart() that crashed the plugin.
- **Systematic Hardening**: Performed a file-by-file audit and hardening of ALL 14 classes (Barbarian, Necromancer, Paladin, Mage, Ranger, DwarfEngineer, Shadowblade, DeathWeaver, Rogue, SacredWarrior, Hammerstorm, Shapeshifter, SilentAssassin, Tinker) to prevent NullReferenceExceptions during pawn death/disconnect.
- **Thread Safety**: Fixed race conditions in `ChangeClass` by ensuring all game state mutations are wrapped in `Server.NextFrame()`.
- **Core Improvements**: Hardened `EventSystem`, `Warcraft` helpers, and `EffectManager` with robust validity checks for player pawns and services.
- **Item Fixes**: Resolved crashes in `Amulet of the Cat` and `Gloves of Cloud`.
- **Shadowblade World Damage**: Fixed crash when taking fall/fire damage by adding null checks for attacker in `PlayerHurt` handler.
- **Zombie Lifecycle**: Fixed NullReferenceException in zombie updates after owner death by adding early return and robust pawn checks.
- **DeathWeaver Resurrection**: Fixed timing issue where teleport could fail due to pawn not being ready after `Respawn()` by wrapping in `Server.NextFrame()`.

ðŸ“¦ Patch Notes â€” Release 2025-11-21
ðŸŽ® Gameplay & AI
Smart Bots: Bots now evaluate nearby threats/allies and trigger ultimates on their own (burst buffs when enemies push, revives when teammates fall, summons/arrowstorms when enemies group up), making PvE lobbies far less passive.
Instant Class Swaps: Requested class changes now execute immediately upon death, so swapping races mid-round no longer waits for the next spawn/round start.
Data Persistence: Disconnecting while controlling a bot now saves the playerâ€™s Warcraft progress instead of skipping the database update, preventing loadout loss when !takeover is active.
New Player Defaults: Set default class to 'ranger' for new players.
âš™ï¸ Config & Menu Systems
Bot Configuration: Added EnableBotUltimates config toggle so server owners can instantly disable the new bot-ultimate logic for niche PvBots/PvP setups without touching code.
Unified Menus: Replaced the old WASD UI with the latest CS2MenuManager WASD menu implementation so all menus now match upstream behavior and respect the Managerâ€™s config options.
Menu Polish: Embedded the CS2MenuManager config inside the plugin and suppressed stale â€œActive benefitsâ€ spam while a race swap is queued so players only see the new class summary.
Unlock Logic: Class selection menu treats total level requirements as inclusive, so races unlock the moment the configured account-wide threshold is reached instead of forcing players to exceed it.
Diagnostics: Added the cooldown.test admin command to run an in-game CooldownManager diagnostic (multi-timer expiry, reset validation) so regressions can be caught without external test harnesses.
ðŸ§™ Class Changes & Hero Fixes
Barbarian: Throwing Axe effect now validates the projectile before cleanup, preventing NullReference spam when the entity is removed early.
Dwarf Engineer: Fixed potential crash in Build ability when the player disconnects.
Tinker: Fixed Ultimate timer not stopping correctly on death/round end.
Ranger: Added safety checks for Ensnare Trap.
Mage: Added validity checks for Mana Shield and Freeze effects.
Necromancer: Added safety check for Cheat Death timer.
Rogue: Added safety check for Smokebomb timer.
Shapeshifter: Added safety checks for Clone Decoy effect.
Shadowblade: Fixed indentation issues in Shadowstep logic.
ðŸ§© Codebase, API & Refactoring
Smoke Compatibility: Custom smoke spawns now set thrower handles and detonation vectors via schema writes, keeping the build compatible with the CounterStrikeSharp update that made Thrower/SmokeDetonationPos read-only.
API Fix: Pawn/controller lookups now explicitly cast the smoke thrower from CCSPlayerPawn.Controller to a CCSPlayerController, eliminating the CBasePlayerController.PlayerPawn compile break on the latest API.
Event Hooks: Dynamic class event listeners now register with their requested hook modes instead of always posting, so pre-hooks (e.g., defensive abilities) fire at the intended point in the engine pipeline.
Shared Logic:
Added a shared GiveWeapon<T> helper so grenade/weapon setup across classes runs through one code path instead of duplicating GiveNamedItem glue.
XP/skill point bookkeeping now lives in AbilityProgression, sharing logic between the XP system, menu UI, and botsâ€”no more ad-hoc free-point math scattered around the codebase.
Menu/UI scaffolding now runs through MenuBuilder, reusing shared builders for pagination/options.
Effect-heavy classes can now piggyback on the new delegate-based EffectBuilder for simple timed buffs (e.g., Rogue/Shadowblade invisibility).
RNG Standardization: All random chance rolls (abilities, items, summons) now route through centralized helpers, ensuring consistent probabilities and making future testing/seeding easier.
Fluent Binders: Hero classes register events/abilities through new fluent binders, eliminating dozens of repetitive HookEvent/HookAbility lines and keeping future classes consistent.
Resource Pre-caching: Custom hero folders can now ship .resources/resources.txt manifests that we precache automatically, keeping model/particle props network-safe after live hero updates.
âš¡ Database & Optimization
Async Operations: Converted database operations to asynchronous (async/await) to prevent main thread blocking.
Thread Safety: Implemented SemaphoreSlim for thread-safe SQLite connection handling and switched WarcraftPlayers to ConcurrentDictionary to prevent threading issues.
Event Handlers: Updated event handlers to support asynchronous player loading and saving.
Stability: Resolved potential server lag during player connect/disconnect and round end saves.
Main Thread Execution: Refactored ChangeClass to execute game state mutations on the main thread to fix concurrency issues.
Error Handling:
Added error handling to OnClientPutInServerHandler and ShowClassMenu to prevent server crashes on database errors.
Fixed NullReferenceException in ClassMenu when player data is missing.
Added logging to identify issues with player data loading.
ðŸ› ï¸ General Fixes
Cooldown Manager: Now validates the owning player and ability before firing ready effects, removing stale entries instead of calling PrintToCenter on invalid entities and spamming Guard.IsValidEntity errors.
Class Swapping: Mid-round class changes now fully reset the previous race (effects/cooldowns) and validate the requested race before instantiation, preventing lingering buffs or invalid class swaps.
State Reversion: Added error handling and state reversion to ChangeClass to prevent data corruption if a class change fails.
Database Integrity:
Fixed SteamID type mismatch (ulong vs long) causing data load failures.
Added null checks and logging to LoadPlayerFromDatabase to prevent crashes and track issues.
Ensured default class fallback is persisted correctly.
