📦 **Warcraft 4.1.0 — Massive Database, Stability, & Fixes Update** (2026-05-17)

💾 **Persistence Refactor**
- Dirty-player saves replaced per-event SQLite writes, so kill XP, assists, bomb rewards, tomes, and skill changes now update memory first and persist through scheduled flush points.
- All SQLite reads and writes now run through one dedicated background dispatcher that owns the connection instead of fire-and-forget gameplay-thread calls.
- Autosave, round-end, map-end, and unload persistence now flush only dirty players in transactional batches instead of queueing one save task per connected player.
- Player and race progress writes now use SQLite UPSERT statements, removing the old existence-check plus insert/update pattern and reducing query overhead.
- Added SQLite tuning with WAL, synchronous=NORMAL, and usy_timeout=5000 to improve write behavior under load.
- Class change, disconnect, class-menu reads, map end, and unload now use barrier flushes where correctness matters so progress stays consistent without restoring hot-path DB pressure.
- Added SaveIntervalSeconds config with a default of 120; set it to ␀ to disable periodic autosave entirely.
- Added persistence diagnostics for dirty-count, batch size, queue depth, flush reason, and flush duration to make frame-time and save-pressure issues easier to trace.

🛡️ **Safety, Stability & Runtime Hardening**
- Fixed !resetskills and !factoryreset crashes when player data or live pawns are missing.
- !factoryreset now skips forced suicide for dead or spectating players and shows safe feedback instead of touching an invalid pawn.
- Reworked disconnect persistence to capture a final player snapshot and queue a non-blocking save instead of stalling the pre-disconnect hook on SQLite.
- Reduced map-end and unload database barrier timeouts to 3 seconds and added timeout diagnostics with dirty-count and queue-depth logging.
- Fixed lethal bonus-damage handling so fatal extra damage now goes through scripted damage and triggers the normal CS2 death sequence.
- Moved async class-menu display back onto the main thread and added shared fire-and-forget error observation for deferred class-change and persistence work.
- Fixed an XP persistence edge case where reaching max level could return before the player was marked dirty.
- Removed Ranger dash debug chat spam from players and routed that diagnostics output through the plugin debug log path instead.
- Fixed plugin instance lifecycle on load/unload and disposed effect/cooldown systems during unload.
- Replaced unobserved sync void client loading with observed fire-and-forget task handling.
- Invalidated cached player snapshots on map and client lifecycle events.
- Updated skill reset/bot autospend paths to use shared AbilityProgression helpers.

⚡ **Performance & Runtime Optimizations**
- Cached GetAllClasses() results instead of allocating a fresh array on every lookup.
- Replaced cooldown-manager ToArray() copies with reusable scratch iteration to reduce tick-time allocations.
- Reused radar player lookups and skip radar scans entirely when no class listens for spotted-enemy custom events.
- Replaced synchronous write-through log flushing with a buffered background logger while keeping the same log files and breadcrumb outputs.
- Added pruning for stale bot-ultimate evaluation handles so long bot-heavy sessions do not accumulate dead entries.
- Replaced Tinker Drone Swarm's 0.01s repeating orbit timer with the existing drone tick update.
- Reduced Ranger Arrowstorm visual projectile/timer pressure while preserving its damage cadence.
- Cached race ability lists so hot paths do not allocate a fresh list on every access.
- Added safer entity creation and game-thread scheduling helpers for delayed runtime work.
- Fixed cleanup warnings for Ranger dash storage, WarcraftPlayer index storage, and Amulet owner capture.

⚔️ **Damage & Event Correctness**
- Moved Talisman of Evasion to victim-side hurt handling so it evades incoming damage instead of cancelling the owner's outgoing damage.
- Fixed Deathbound Bulwark to restore prevented health and armor on the live pawn, matching the real damage-cancellation path.
- Kept victim defensive class and item hooks running on lethal player_hurt events.
- Replaced attacker-wide same-tick hurt suppression with shotgun-only dedupe keyed by attacker, victim, weapon, and tick.
- Kept victim death cleanup, effect destruction, weapon insurance, and pending class-change handling active for world/null-attacker deaths.

🎯 **Race, Item, & Effect Hardening**
- Fixed Rogue Smokebomb lethal checks and backstab angle wraparound.
- Fixed Dagger of Venom poison refresh so item poison is keyed by owner/source and no longer blocks unrelated Shadowblade poison.
- Hardened Dwarf Engineer pickup flags and delayed entity callbacks.
- Filtered Shapeshifter weapon restore lists to skip invalid handles, C4, knives, tasers, and temporary utility.
- Made Amulet of the Cat track and reset silent-footstep hook state during bulk cleanup.
- Made effect disposal/map-end cleanup finish effects so state contributions and hooks are removed.
- Hardened EffectManager with disposal, callback exception logging, invalid-owner pruning, and no-tick passive effects.
- Added per-tick PlayerCache reuse for aura, AoE, radar, advert, and bot scanning paths.
- Consolidated glove grenade refill logic into reusable GrenadeSupplyEffect.
- Updated embedded CS2MenuManager WASD menu behavior to preserve menu state across close/choose and clean stale state on disconnect/round end.

🛠️ **Version, Testing, & Dependencies**
- Bumped ModuleVersion, assembly version, and package version to 4.1.0.
- Updated CounterStrikeSharp.API to 1.0.368 and refreshed stable package patches, including explicit System.Text.Json 10.0.8.
- Removed stale packages.config.
- Made the Release deploy copy path configurable with WarcraftPluginDeployDir instead of copying to a hard-coded server folder.
- Kept vendored CS2MenuManager's Tomlyn dependency at ␀.19.0 because upstream CS2MenuManager v1.0.42 still uses that API.
- Added WarcraftPlugin.Tests with coverage for ability progression, persistence dirty-version handling, SQLite dispatcher ordering/drain completion, duplicate item prevention, and class unlock thresholds.
- Verified Debug build, Release build, tests, formatter, vulnerable package scan, and outdated package scan.
- Added unit coverage for damage reduction math, angle wraparound, weapon normalization, shotgun hurt dedupe, and Shapeshifter weapon filtering.

