Warcraft 4.1.1 Class Change Hotfix - 2026-05-26
- Bumped ModuleVersion, assembly version, package version, and version.txt to 4.1.1.
- Fixed queued race/class changes so menu selections while dead or alive wait for the next round spawn instead of applying immediately on death or same-round respawn.
- Added explicit queued class-change readiness state, marked at round end and consumed on the next spawn.
- Fixed non-main-thread CounterStrikeSharp native access in async class-change error logging by capturing player identity before awaits and using captured values after database work.
- Added database helper overloads for class-change persistence that use captured SteamID/name instead of reading controller native properties after async awaits.
- Added unit coverage for queued class-change readiness.
- Fixed ultimate command handling during bot takeover by resolving the active bot controller through CounterStrikeSharp's takeover state, using the bot's Warcraft state for the ability, and keeping feedback on the human client.
- Added null guards and exception logging around ultimate invocation so missing Warcraft state or an ability failure logs cleanly instead of crashing the server.

Warcraft 4.1.1 Bot-Control and Stability Hotfix - 2026-05-26
- Kept version fields at 4.1.1 for the same-release hotfix.
- Hardened bot-takeover ultimate resolution so controlled-bot ultimates use the bot Warcraft state and fail safely when the bot controller cannot be resolved.
- Added revive-target filtering so bot-controlled Paladin and Death Weaver ultimates cannot revive the human currently controlling that bot.
- Fixed Rogue Smokebomb cheat-death to run from the death event, respawn safely, and force an instant smoke cloud instead of leaving a bouncing smoke projectile.
- Added stable WarcraftPlayer identity cleanup for disconnects, including captured slot, controller handle, and SteamID.
- Hardened Drone, Zombie, and Necromancer summon cleanup against invalid owners, removed entities, failed spawns, and race changes.
- Restored class appearance safely after Mage freeze and Barbarian bloodlust instead of resetting players to plain white.
- Added health/armor state replication after direct damage-helper mutations.
- Added ConfigureAwait(false) to SQLite dispatcher/database awaits used by map-end and unload barriers.
- Clamped Shadowblade Evasion and Shadowstep rolls to valid skill levels and skipped no-damage events so corrupted/oversized ability data cannot make the race effectively unkillable.
- Added safe state-change replication for helper-driven color, health, armor, adrenaline, and delayed scale updates to avoid unobserved invalid-entity exceptions after entities are removed.
- Fixed Mage, Necromancer, and Dwarf Engineer grenade grants by using the correct base weapon wrapper for molotov, smoke, and grenade entities.
- Reworked Hammerstorm Warcry health through derived max-health state so bonus health survives normal damage/heal interactions and resets cleanly.
- Reworked Rogue Smokebomb stun through derived speed/max-speed state and stopped invulnerability hits from forcing healed players back to 1 HP.
- Restored live pawn speed, gravity, max speed, and max health when derived player state is reset on spawn/class cleanup.
- Enabled Tinker attack drone rocket rolls at 10% per drone level on the first shot of each volley.
- Changed Mage ultimate behavior from Arcane Dash to Teleport to match localization and updated the race wiki entry.
- Added Warcraft menu readability preferences with configurable default menu scale/type, player `!wcmenu` settings, SQLite preference persistence, and scaled race/shop/skills menu rendering.
- Bumped ConfigVersion to 12 for the new menu display configuration fields while keeping plugin version fields unchanged.

Warcraft Unreleased - 2026-07-10
- Migrated the plugin and test projects to `net10.0` and updated `CounterStrikeSharp.API` to `1.0.370`; deployment now requires the matching CounterStrikeSharp 1.0.370 runtime.
- Pinned `SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3` to `3.53.3`, replacing the vulnerable transitive native SQLite package reported by the dependency scan.
- Added the root-admin `!perf.capture [seconds]` diagnostic. It captures Warcraft tick/event min, average, p95, and max timings plus active effects, drones, invisibility entries, player count, dirty-player count, and SQLite queue depth in the persistent log. Captures are opt-in and default to 60 seconds.
- Replaced one `OnTick` listener per Tinker with a single lifecycle-managed drone scheduler and cleaned it up on drone deactivation, map end, and plugin unload.
- Removed recurring LINQ/list allocations from bot-ultimate scheduling, invisibility transmit snapshots, drone target scans, Ranger Arrowstorm, and Necromancer poison-cloud scans while preserving their target-selection and gameplay behavior.
- Added rate-limited warnings for sustained SQLite dispatcher queue pressure without dropping or reordering player-progress writes.
- Added regression coverage for performance statistics and queue-pressure warning thresholds. Automated validation passed: Debug build, Release build, format verification, vulnerability scan, and 52 tests. Manual 20-player server validation and matching CounterStrikeSharp runtime deployment are required before release.
- Fixed Warcraft menu lifecycle races that could leave stale menu instances alive after rapid close/reopen actions. Pending next-frame opens now use a per-player generation guard, old expiry timers cannot close a newer menu, and active menus are closed on round end, map end, disconnect, and plugin unload.
- Made Warcraft's menu type preference apply to class, skills, shop, and settings menus. Selecting ConsoleMenu is now a real renderer isolation test instead of silently opening the WASD center-HTML menu.
- Added menu-session regression coverage. Automated validation after the menu fix passed: Debug build, Release build, format verification, and 54 tests. Manual test-server validation of repeated `!class`/`!skills` open-close-open cycles is required before release.
